study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-037-wave-34/item-T205-observe-plan.md:47:**Motion findings (A10.3 form; REVISED on codex-observe G-T205-3 with fine probes at 43.2/43.4/43.6/43.8 s, census now 27 frames):** Motion instants: outline draw-on 37–39 s · layout shift ≤39–40 s (between census frames; sub-second, priced as ≤1000 ms) · ballot paper growth + check draw 40–43 s · connector extension 42–43.2 s · **paper RETRACT at ~43.2 s (the ballot drops into the box — the casting beat)** · paper reappear-high + check recolour + **GRADED block wash 43.4–44.0 s** (pale at 43.6, full by 44.0 — a ~600 ms eased wash of ONE block whole, not squares lighting sequentially) · global fade-out 45–46 s. Holds: substrate complete 39–40 s (~1 s) · pre-connector diagram 40–42 s · converted state 44–46 s (~2 s, incl. fade onset). Dissolve: the diagram never exits by parts — it fades globally to a pale wash under the incoming portrait (46 s frame). Sub-beats: (i) substrate draw-on is the T204/T210 shared grid, not conversion motion; (ii) the retract→reappear is the conversion's causal hinge: vote cast (paper in) → allocation appears (paper back up, checked red, block washing); (iii) only ONE block ever fills in this window. Correction (codex-observe G-T205-1): the 36.0 s pre-window frame carries the preceding title beat, not only drawing outlines — its table description stands corrected here.
study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-037-wave-34/item-T205-observe-plan.md:50:- G-T205-1 (window overstatement): digest claims 0:37–1:00 (23 s) for this technique; the census shows the conversion diagram lives 37.0–46.0 s (9.0 s). 46–60 s is a portrait-carousel consequence beat (different visual technique, photographic content — not recreatable as this technique and not part of it). Plan therefore cuts 37.0–46.0 s (see §2).
study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-037-wave-34/item-T205-observe-plan.md:51:- G-T205-2 (evidence frame does not depict the technique): the digest's sole cited evidence frame ev/t52-vote-to-grid.jpg is byte-identical to census 52.0 s (SHA-256 c4e480893d4c2851e16b71eca756a5f9e658eac6ed668c05d0214fa13e2c7b1f, verified by hash equality) and shows the three portraits, NOT the ballot→grid diagram. The technique's true evidence frames are this census's 40/43/44 s frames. Observe proceeds on the census, not the cited frame.
study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-037-wave-34/item-T205-observe-plan.md:52:- G-T205-3 (fill granularity): digest/TECHNIQUES prose ("a grid fills in blocks", "fills red in blocks") is ambiguous between per-square and per-block fill; census resolves it: per-BLOCK wash (one state block at a time), squares unchanged on top. Plan binds per-block.
study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-037-wave-34/item-T205-observe-plan.md:58:Diagram containers — the DLC assembler's count-board / diagram surface. Priced: the assembler's core need is exactly this operation — an input (a vote, a count, a choice) entering one side and exiting as allocated blocks whose whole-block flip carries the argument (digest §2: block-weighted count board; §6 L1/L4). T205 is the minimal pure form of that operation (one input → one block) with no tally arithmetic on top, so it is the reusable primitive the count-board family composes; T53's board already proves the composed form passes (85.6). Secondary: explainer production's mechanism-diagram beats.
